==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.07~1 seconds<sup>2f~30f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~1 seconds<sup>2f~30f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~1 seconds<sup>2f~30f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 0.07~1 seconds<sup>2f~30f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 0.07~3 seconds<sup>2f~90f</sup>.
*4 [[Tackey]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The combination of buffed R.Osts to chop down your meatshields and Tackeys to take out chunks of your ranged units is quite formidable. Perhaps the sole consolation is that money will ''never'' be a problem here because of the massive and constant stream of peons, which means that [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] is almost required to clear out waves of weak enemies and refill your wallet. In higher difficulties you must rush them with both [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] and [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Grandmaster Cat]] in the absence of a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], or face the stronger R.Osts with properly protected [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborgs]]. [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] will prove useful, as the only non-Traitless enemy here is Tackey.
As seen in the walkthrough by yohane this stage can be easily rushed with [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and [[Mr. (Special Cat)|Hyper Mr.]]

A way to beat this stage on 4-crown difficulty is to use the peons as stepping stones for [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Cat's]] explosion to juggle the [[R.Ost|R.ost]].

